  "question": {
    "text": "Let a circle $C$ pass through the points $(4,2)$ and $(0,2)$, and its centre lie on $3 x+2 y+2=0$. Then the length of the chord, of the circle $C$, whose mid-point is $(1,2)$, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vq2xy",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1mxB3",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TxQ2Q",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1coeH",
      "text": "$4 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the centre be\n$\\left(-2 a, \\frac{6 a-2}{2}\\right) \\equiv(-2 a, 3 a-1)$\nCentre is equal distance from $(4,2)$ and $(0,2)$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{(4+2 a)^2+(3 a-3)^2}=\\sqrt{(-2 a-0)^2+(3 a-3)^2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow(2 a+4)^2+9(a-1)^2=4 a^2+9(a-1)^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 4 a^2+16+16 a=4 a^2 \\Rightarrow a=-1 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\text { centre } \\equiv(2,-4) \\Rightarrow \\text { Radius }=\\sqrt{40}\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/mo9pueNhdhDjU0vQBlqBS9Zz8Vbf34maYFKLjR5TvbM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow A M^2=(\\sqrt{40})^2-(\\sqrt{37})^2 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 2 A M=A B=2 \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
